To add a Gaussian filter before applying the Sobel operator, you need to create a Gaussian kernel with a certain standard deviation (sigma) and convolve it with the input image using the `filter2` function in MATLAB. Here's how you can modify your existing code to achieve this:

```matlab
% Load the input image
input_image = imread('image.jpg');

% Define the size of the Gaussian kernel
kernel_size = [13 13];

% Define the standard deviation of the Gaussian kernel
sigma = 2;

% Create the Gaussian kernel
[gaussian_kernel, gaussian_coef] = fspecial('gaussian', kernel_size, sigma);

% Convolve the input image with the Gaussian kernel
blurred_image = filter2(double(input_image), gaussian_kernel, 'replicate');

% Convert the blurred image to grayscale
gray_image = rgb2gray(blurred_image);

% Define the Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];

% Apply the Sobel operator to the blurred image in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(gray_image), sobel_x, 'same');

% Apply the Sobel operator to the blurred image in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(gray_image), sobel_y, 'same');

% Combine the edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);

% Display the resulting edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```

